<<if $gotpole>>
	<<jump PoleGotDialogue>>
<<endif>> 
<< LightOff RadioLight >>
SETTING - Beneath the stained glass window in the Solster Train Station.

AT RISE - SASHA's radio blares a grating noise that echoes through the entire hallway.

NARRATOR: [i]This[/i] is [i]your[/i] radio. You thought that the kids who nicked it off of you would've sold it by now already, but it seems they were more intent on mischief rather than petty thievery.

-> Thank god it's still here, how do I get it back?
NARRATOR: It's laid close enough to the edge of the construction platform that you could potentially knock it down with some maneuvering and focus.
NARRATOR: Or.. maybe someone could get it down for you? You don't want the radio to shatter, after all.

-> Who even [i]were[/i] those kids?
	NARRATOR: You didn't know them. Either they were babies when you left, or you didn't spend enough time with the children of this town.
-> The nerve..

<<if $ArtMajor == true>>
		ART: All of it causes the need for some.. [i]creative[/i] thinking, heh heh.
	<<elseif $TechMajor == true>>
		TECH: This is ridiculous, where's the construction men? Surely they have some sort of doohickey.
	<<elseif $PsychMajor == true>>
		PSY: I hope none of the people around it realize it's mine. This sound is rather.. infuriating.
	<<endif>>
<<set $RadioStopQuest = true>>
<<LightOn LanternShop>>
===
title: PoleGotDialogue
